        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0777" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg653"/>

                <head>No. 413.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Marsh</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 18,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 749.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge with thanks the
                    receipt of your No. 922, having reference to the high qualities which
                    distinguished the late Baron Bettino Ricasoli, former prime minister of Italy;
                    as also to his friendship for the United States.</p>
                <p>The estimable qualities of Baron Ricasoli, and his attitude toward this country
                    at a critical period in its history, combine to render his decease a subject of
                    sympathy and regret to the good citizens of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
